756
01:40:06.658 --> 01:40:09.658
That is not something vague, something unreachable.

757
01:40:09.658 --> 01:40:12.658
Or in a certain way, also unreachable.

758
01:40:12.658 --> 01:40:20.658
But holy means completely set apart, completely separated from everything that is not perfect.

759
01:40:20.658 --> 01:40:31.658
And this was God's way of showing us how holy he is, how serious it is.

760
01:40:31.658 --> 01:40:37.658
So he had given the whole law and it is not like, okay here is the law, do your best.

761
01:40:37.658 --> 01:40:39.658
Shall we see how far you get.

762
01:40:39.658 --> 01:40:47.658
No, here God clearly indicates through the law, through the tabernacle, through the priestly service, through the offerings.

763
01:40:47.658 --> 01:40:56.658
That it is very serious, how serious the holiness of God is, how serious it is.

764
01:40:56.658 --> 01:41:02.658
How you absolutely cannot just throw it aside and mess around a bit.

765
01:41:02.658 --> 01:41:09.658
How you cannot even do your best, how you cannot even do your utmost best.

766
01:41:09.658 --> 01:41:11.658
Nothing is enough for God.

767
01:41:11.658 --> 01:41:22.658
Somewhere you go wrong and become separated from God because your mistakes cannot coexist with God.

768
01:41:22.658 --> 01:41:27.658
And all this clearly indicates.

769
01:41:27.658 --> 01:41:37.658
That meant that actually it was impossible for the people of Israel to come close to God, to be intimate with Him.

770
01:41:42.658 --> 01:41:44.658
And what about us?

771
01:41:44.658 --> 01:41:54.658
Why are we here now in Lommel, in 2023, in a church, worshiping God

772
01:41:54.658 --> 01:42:02.658
and pretending that we can be intimate with Him, as if we may talk to Him, sing songs to Him?

773
01:42:02.658 --> 01:42:05.658
What has changed?

774
01:42:05.658 --> 01:42:09.658
Well, I will tell you, one thing has not changed.

775
01:42:09.658 --> 01:42:11.658
And that is God.

776
01:42:12.658 --> 01:42:15.658
God is still, right now, today here.

777
01:42:15.658 --> 01:42:23.658
Exactly the same God as at the tabernacle then, as at the laws then, as at the offerings then.

778
01:42:23.658 --> 01:42:25.658
Exactly the same God.

779
01:42:25.658 --> 01:42:31.658
He did not at some point in history say, you know what, people cannot handle it,

780
01:42:31.658 --> 01:42:38.658
laws are way too difficult, we will water it down a bit, if they do their best then it will be fine.

781
01:42:38.658 --> 01:42:47.658
No, absolutely not. God is still that same holy God who cannot have even a millimeter of communion

782
01:42:47.658 --> 01:42:50.658
with people who are covered in sin.

783
01:42:50.658 --> 01:42:52.658
What has happened then?

784
01:42:52.658 --> 01:42:56.658
There is a small hint here on the podium.

785
01:42:56.658 --> 01:42:58.658
We will read about that.

786
01:42:58.658 --> 01:43:03.658
Very nice for this week, Friday is Good Friday.

787
01:43:03.658 --> 01:43:10.658
The day on which we celebrate, however strange that word may sound in this context,

788
01:43:10.658 --> 01:43:15.658
but we are going to celebrate that Jesus died on the cross for us.

789
01:43:15.658 --> 01:43:20.658
And we will read about that in Matthew 27.

790
01:43:20.658 --> 01:43:24.658
So Jesus is hanging on the cross.

791
01:43:24.658 --> 01:43:31.658
At about twelve o'clock it became completely dark over the whole land.

792
01:43:31.658 --> 01:43:34.658
It lasted until about three o'clock in the afternoon.

793
01:43:34.658 --> 01:43:36.658
Then Jesus cried out loudly,

794
01:43:36.658 --> 01:43:45.658
Eli, Eli, lama samachtani, which means my God, my God, why have You forsaken me?

795
01:43:45.658 --> 01:43:50.658
A few people standing there said, oh, he is calling Elijah.

796
01:43:50.658 --> 01:43:58.658
One of the people ran to Jesus, soaked a sponge in sour wine, put it on a stick, and gave him to drink.

797
01:43:58.658 --> 01:44:04.658
But others said, don't do that, let's see if Elijah comes to save him.

798
01:44:04.658 --> 01:44:16.658
But Jesus gave a loud cry and died.

799
01:44:16.658 --> 01:44:25.658
At that moment, the curtain in the temple was torn in two from top to bottom.

800
01:44:25.658 --> 01:44:31.658
That veil that we had seen between the holy and the most holy place,

801
01:44:31.658 --> 01:44:36.658
that curtain of ten meters high tore,

802
01:44:36.658 --> 01:44:44.658
at the moment when Jesus died on the cross, into two pieces.

803
01:44:44.658 --> 01:44:49.658
What happened there, indescribable.

804
01:44:49.658 --> 01:45:02.658
All those laws, all that tabernacle, all those sacrifices, that priestly service, were completely turned upside down at that moment.

805
01:45:02.658 --> 01:45:10.658
The curtain that separated the people of Israel from God,

806
01:45:10.658 --> 01:45:18.658
