807
01:45:18.658 --> 01:45:20.658
Was open.

808
01:45:20.658 --> 01:45:25.658
Which indicates that something drastic has changed.

809
01:45:25.658 --> 01:45:30.658
For suddenly that curtain is no longer in our way.

810
01:45:30.658 --> 01:45:36.658
Suddenly we can come into that holiness with God.

811
01:45:36.658 --> 01:45:39.658
By that ark with the ten commandments in it.

812
01:45:39.658 --> 01:45:42.658
By that cloud and pillar of fire that is above.

813
01:45:42.658 --> 01:45:48.658
Suddenly something has changed, because Jesus dies there,

814
01:45:48.658 --> 01:45:51.658
which allows us to come to him.

815
01:45:51.658 --> 01:45:58.658
Which means we are suddenly no longer forbidden to enter there with him.

816
01:45:58.658 --> 01:46:08.658
That is of course because at that moment Jesus took upon himself all sins, all our mistakes, all our righteousness.

817
01:46:08.658 --> 01:46:16.658
Like that little lamb, which the Israelites could offer by laying a hand on the lamb.

818
01:46:16.658 --> 01:46:23.658
And then the entire guilt of the people symbolically came upon the lamb.

819
01:46:23.658 --> 01:46:34.658
So Jesus said, it was as if at that moment when Jesus was on the Cross we laid our hand on Jesus.

820
01:46:34.658 --> 01:46:36.658
And all our guilt came upon him.

821
01:46:36.658 --> 01:46:40.658
Not anymore symbolic, but real.

822
01:46:40.658 --> 01:46:47.658
And he said, I take all that guilt upon myself and I die in your place.

823
01:46:47.658 --> 01:46:51.658
Just as in the tabernacle that little lamb died.

824
01:46:51.658 --> 01:46:53.658
Because of our guilt.

825
01:46:53.658 --> 01:46:58.658
Thus Jesus died because of our guilt.

826
01:46:58.658 --> 01:47:05.658
We should have died, but Jesus died for us.

827
01:47:05.658 --> 01:47:13.658
And the reason he could do that and still live is of course because he was God.

828
01:47:13.658 --> 01:47:18.658
But because he was obedient to God.

829
01:47:18.658 --> 01:47:21.658
For what is this whole story really about?

830
01:47:21.658 --> 01:47:24.658
This story is about obedience.

831
01:47:24.658 --> 01:47:27.658
God is not at all interested in sacrifices.

832
01:47:27.658 --> 01:47:33.658
In sacrificing a little lamb, or in sprinkling blood, or in all those actions.

833
01:47:33.658 --> 01:47:35.658
That is not what God is after at all.

834
01:47:35.658 --> 01:47:38.658
Why did God give the law?

835
01:47:38.658 --> 01:47:44.658
Not to chase us into a harness of, I want it to happen this way, so it will happen that way.

836
01:47:44.658 --> 01:47:46.658
No, because God is the Creator.

837
01:47:46.658 --> 01:47:48.658
He made everything.

838
01:47:48.658 --> 01:47:50.658
He knows exactly how we should live.

839
01:47:50.658 --> 01:47:57.658
He knows exactly that if we live in a certain way or not, it will go well with us.

840
01:47:57.658 --> 01:47:59.658
And that he is honored.

841
01:47:59.658 --> 01:48:05.658
So God is interested in obedience.

842
01:48:05.658 --> 01:48:10.658
That was already the case back then, you could clearly see that from all those precise rules.

843
01:48:10.658 --> 01:48:15.658
It was meant to lead people towards obedience to Him.

844
01:48:15.658 --> 01:48:19.658
And as I said, God has not changed one millimeter.

845
01:48:19.658 --> 01:48:21.658
That is still the case today.

846
01:48:21.658 --> 01:48:25.658
But Jesus was perfectly obedient.

847
01:48:25.658 --> 01:48:27.658
And that is why He was without guilt.

848
01:48:27.658 --> 01:48:30.658
That is why He could come to the Father.

849
01:48:30.658 --> 01:48:35.658
But He took all our guilt upon Himself and died in our place.

850
01:48:35.658 --> 01:48:37.658
And with that, we were set free.

851
01:48:39.658 --> 01:48:43.658
Then we continue in Hebrews 10.

852
01:48:43.658 --> 01:48:48.658
We have already made significant progress this week...

853
